@* The live link in the page's bar (passata grafica, 2026-09-29): a pill with a dot and a word. Up and
   well, a grey "Live" with a green dot - until then the page said nothing at all in that case. Not
   well, the pill takes the tone of what is wrong (orange while it connects, or when the canvas
   cannot draw it or a part of it stopped working; red when the link is down or could not even be
   built), and the sentence the page used to show as a line is inside it, word for word, behind a
   tip that the mouse or the keyboard's focus opens - and the pill's description for a screen reader
   (aria-describedby: hidden, the tip is out of the accessibility tree, and the pill would say its
   word and never why). What a failure on this side threw - its type and message - is in the tip too,
   under the sentence and apart from it (row 37 of the queue, extended to the whole page on 10/10):
   the pill has no room for a "?", and its tip is already what opens on demand. The one case that asks the operator to act - a channel that could not be
   built, which only a reload tries again - is also a red line of the row of outcomes under the bar
   (UnavailableNoticeOf): a tip nobody opens tells nobody to reload. *@
@using Wcs.WebEditor.Live

@if (Look is { } look)
{
    if (Line is { } line)
    {
        <span id="drawio-live-status" class="drawio-pill @look.Tone drawio-has-tip" tabindex="0" aria-describedby="drawio-live-status-tip"><DrawioIcon Name="live" />@look.Word<span id="drawio-live-status-tip" class="drawio-tip" role="tooltip"><span id="drawio-live-status-sentence">@line</span>@if (Detail is { } detail)
        {
            <span id="drawio-live-status-detail" class="drawio-failure-detail">@detail</span>
        }</span></span>
    }
    else
    {
        <span id="drawio-live-status" class="drawio-pill @look.Tone drawio-live-on"><DrawioIcon Name="live" />@look.Word</span>
    }
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public LiveConnection? Connection { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public bool DrawFailed { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What was thrown, when the failure was on the page's side and the browser console cannot say it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? DrawFailedReason { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What was thrown when the page could not even build its channel to the host, if it could not: then there is no Connection at all.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Unavailable { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A part of the live status that stopped working (the hover toggle, for one), already worded by the page.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Trouble { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What was thrown behind <see cref="Trouble"/>, if anything: in the tip under the sentence.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? TroubleDetail { get; set; }

    private string? Line => Connection switch
    {
        _ when Unavailable is not null => UnavailableSentence,
        LiveConnection.Interrupted =>
            "Live status is not being updated: the connection to the host is interrupted, and the colours and arrows on the drawing are the last ones received. The page tries again by itself.",
        LiveConnection.Connecting => "Live status: connecting to the host...",
        _ when DrawFailed => DrawFailedReason is null
            ? "Live status cannot be drawn on this canvas (the browser console says why): the drawing and the save work as before."
            : "Live status cannot be drawn on this canvas: the drawing and the save work as before.",
        _ => Trouble,
    };

    /// <summary>What was thrown behind <see cref="Line"/>, in the order of its cases; null when the line says no failure of this side.</summary>
    private string? Detail => Connection switch
    {
        _ when Unavailable is { } thrown => thrown,
        LiveConnection.Interrupted or LiveConnection.Connecting => null,
        _ when DrawFailed => DrawFailedReason,
        _ => TroubleDetail,
    };

    /// <summary>The pill's word and tone, in the order of <see cref="Line"/>'s cases: there is a pill whenever there is a line, and a quiet one when the link is up and nothing is wrong.</summary>
    private (string Word, string Tone)? Look => Connection switch
    {
        _ when Unavailable is not null => ("Live off", "drawio-pill-bad"),
        LiveConnection.Interrupted => ("Offline", "drawio-pill-bad"),
        LiveConnection.Connecting => ("Connecting", "drawio-pill-warn"),
        _ when DrawFailed => ("Live off", "drawio-pill-warn"),
        _ when Trouble is not null => ("Live", "drawio-pill-warn"),
        LiveConnection.Live => ("Live", "drawio-pill-neutral"),
        _ => null,
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// The channel that could not be built, as a line of the row under the bar: red, and it stays - the
    /// page never tries again by itself, a reload does, and that is the operator's to do. The pill's
    /// sentence whole, as the drawing out of reach is: its end is why it is in the row. What was thrown
    /// is behind the "?" after it (row 37 of the queue, extended to the whole page on 10/10). The link's
    /// other troubles stay behind the pill's tip alone - they mend by themselves (connecting,
    /// interrupted) or leave the drawing and the save as they were (not drawn, a piece that stopped) -
    /// and ask nothing.
    /// </summary>
    public static DrawioNoticeLine? UnavailableNoticeOf(string? unavailable) =>
        unavailable is { } thrown
            ? new DrawioNoticeLine("drawio-live", DrawioNoticeTone.Bad, UnavailableSentence, Dismissable: false, null)
            {
                LineDetail = thrown,
            }
            : null;

    /// <summary>The page's own sentence in English; the exception's text, in whatever language it comes, is apart from it.</summary>
    private const string UnavailableSentence =
        "Live status is not available on this page: the channel to the host could not be opened. The drawing and the save work as before; reload the page to try again.";
}
